      "caption": {
        "known": true,
        "value": "Mask forced on a victim's head to lend torture an extra degree of cruelty.\nIt magnifies one's fears and makes them acutely aware of all forms of pain.\n\nRaises attack power when the wearer suffers from madness.\n\nWhen the Black Dumpling goes on, the torturer no longer seeks answers; only to inflict suffering without hope of relief.",
        "provenance": {
          "source": "legacy_db_data",
          "method": "copied from legacy ItemTexts.Caption"
        }
      },
      "description": {
        "known": true,
        "value": "Red cloth blindfold used to cover prisoners' eyes",
        "provenance": {
          "source": "legacy_db_data",
          "method": "copied from legacy ItemTexts.Description"
        }
      },
      "location": {
        "known": true,
        "value": "The Black Dumpling Helm can be obtained by killing the First Generation Albinaurics found at Volcano Manor and in the lower Leyndell Royal Capital who wear it.; Three Albinaurics can be found close to the Church of the Eclipse Site of Grace in Castle Sol . From the Site, take the South-East door, exit the chappel and go straight ahead inside the tower. Be careful not to get ambushed.; Five Albinaurics can be found just outside the Guest Hall Site of Grace in Volcano Manor",
        "provenance": {
